{"n": 203, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "203.webp", "text": "12-111/8\n\nIDLE SPEED CONTROL, SPEED LIMIT, COLD START CONTROL\nReter to E 34 diagnosis test plan in chapter 1210 OME M 13,\n\nTYPES OF INJECTION\n\nEach group of fuel Injectors (2+ 4 or 1 + 3) Is activated by a final stage (current\namplifier). It ts theretore possible to divide the injection cycle Into groups of\ncylinders. This guarantees limited engine operation even when one group falls.\n\nSemi-sequential injection:\n\nThere Is injection In one group of cylinders (2 + 4 or 1 + 3) only once every 720\ncrankshall degrees as from an engine speed of 600 rpm. This timing can func-\n\ntion only when the DME control unit receives a signal fram the camshall send-\n\ner (on camshaft sprocket of exhaust valves). Timing remains In semi-sequential\nInjection if the signal Is received later.\n\nParallel Injection:\n\nParallel injection means simultaneous activation of all fuel injectors for each\n\nCrankshaft revolution and takes place only when the camshaft sender has not\nput out any signats since starting the engine.\n\nif a signal Is put out later, the system switches over lo semi-sequential injec-\n\ntlon a& $00n as an engine speed of 2500 rpm Is exceeded.\n\nIGNITION\n\nStationary ignition Distribution:\n\nEach cylinder has its own ignition coll. in this manner the sysiem of rotating\nignition distribution Is omitted. DME activates each ignition coll separately.\n\nDouble ignition:\n\nDouble ignition means activation of the spark plugs for éach crankshall revo-\nlution and takes place only when the camshaft sender does not put oul signals.\nSwitching over from normal to double ignition, or vice versa, takes place im-\nmediately in contradiction to fuel injection.\n\nANTL-KNOCK FUNCTION\nThe ignition timing is retarded depending on intake alt and engine temperature,\n\nin order to prevent seif-ignition of the tuelair mixture In the combustion\nchamber (knocking).\n\nCATALYTIC CONVERTER PROTECTION\n\nThere is danger of overheating the catalytic converter when the catalytic con-\nwerter protection Is active over a long period of time. For this reason the fuel |\nalr mixture is enriched to reduce (he exhaust gas temperature.\nTHROTTLE VALVE POTENTIOMETER\n\nA throttie valve potentiometer !s instalied instead of a throttle valve switch with\n\nIdle and tull load contacts, This potentiometer must mo longer be adjusted,\nsince DME learns the Idle speed Ignition timing (idle speed switching point) on\nits own. DME adds a determined value to the learned value. This value must go\nowe potentiometer to OME In order to be processed as a full load signal in\nDM\n\nAIR CONDITIONER COMPRESSOR SHUTOFF\nIn order to have the entire engine power for drive while moving olf, the air\n\nconditioner compressor is switched off for up to 7 seconds at road speeds of\n<8 kevh (5 mph) and simultaneous full load state.\n\nTANK VENTING FOR MODELS WITH CATALYTIC CONVERTER\n\nOXYGEN SENSOR CONTROL FOR MODELS WITH CATALYTIC CONVERTER\nDRIVE AWAY PREVENTION\n\nSELF-DIAGNOSIS\n\nRefer to'E 34 diagnosis test plan in chapter 1210 DME M 1.3 for Inftarmation\nabout the BMW diagnosing system.", "words": [["12-111/8", 0.4683, 0.0283, 0.5714, 0.054], ["IDLE", 0.0302, 0.0882, 0.0563, 0.1001], ["SPEED", 0.0629, 0.0816, 0.0976, 0.1053], ["CONTROL,", 0.1021, 0.0869, 0.2012, 0.1001], ["SPEED", 0.1655, 0.0816, 0.1987, 0.1053], ["LIMIT,", 0.2047, 0.0816, 0.2379, 0.1053], ["COLD", 0.247, 0.0816, 0.2741, 0.1053], ["START", 0.2802, 0.0816, 0.3149, 0.1053], ["CONTROL", 0.3199, 0.0843, 0.3747, 0.0987], ["Reter", 0.0292, 0.1165, 0.0589, 0.1396], ["to", 0.0644, 0.1165, 0.0744, 0.1396], ["E", 0.0805, 0.1218, 0.085, 0.1336], ["34", 0.0905, 0.1165, 0.1011, 0.1396], ["diagnosis", 0.1051, 0.1165, 0.1554, 0.1396], ["test", 0.1595, 0.1165, 0.1806, 0.1396], ["plan", 0.1846, 0.1165, 0.2052, 0.1396], ["in", 0.2113, 0.1218, 0.2208, 0.1323], ["chapter", 0.2269, 0.1165, 0.2671, 0.1396], ["1210", 0.2711, 0.1205, 0.2948, 0.1323], ["OME",